1
00:00:03,052 --> 00:00:05,209
At the museum stands a giant skeleton!

2
00:00:05,259 --> 00:00:08,288
But dinosaurs disappeared a very, very long time ago…

3
00:00:08,338 --> 00:00:10,139
so how do we know they existed?

4
00:00:10,924 --> 00:00:12,834
These bones are not real bones…

5
00:00:12,884 --> 00:00:14,287
they turned into stone!

6
00:00:14,337 --> 00:00:17,624
They're fossils, and Mila finds them cold and heavy.

7
00:00:18,412 --> 00:00:19,926
Discovery mission!

8
00:00:22,442 --> 00:00:23,077
Mini mode!

9
00:00:23,127 --> 00:00:25,066
A dinosaur dies near a river.

10
00:00:25,116 --> 00:00:27,741
Its skin and muscles disappear quickly,

11
00:00:27,791 --> 00:00:31,426
then sand and mud cover its bones, layer after layer.

12
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:35,948
Underground, water seeps into the bones and leaves minerals behind:

13
00:00:35,998 --> 00:00:38,329
the bone turns to stone, little by little.

14
00:00:38,379 --> 00:00:40,929
And above, the layers get squashed into rock.

15
00:00:41,701 --> 00:00:44,337
Millions of years later, the rock wears away,

16
00:00:44,387 --> 00:00:45,711
and the fossil appears.

17
00:00:45,761 --> 00:00:46,427
And its age?

18
00:00:46,477 --> 00:00:48,755
The volcanic ash around it has a clock:

19
00:00:48,805 --> 00:00:50,895
atoms that change at a known speed.

20
00:00:51,698 --> 00:00:53,395
Bones, teeth, footprints, eggs…

21
00:00:53,445 --> 00:00:56,099
there are thousands of fossils around the world!

22
00:00:56,149 --> 00:00:57,846
Becoming a fossil is very rare…

23
00:00:57,896 --> 00:01:00,206
but over millions of years, that adds up!

24
00:01:00,990 --> 00:01:03,767
And that's how we know dinosaurs existed.

25
00:01:04,544 --> 00:01:06,505
Dinosaur bones turned to stone:

26
00:01:06,555 --> 00:01:09,020
fossils are the proof that they lived.

27
00:01:10,041 --> 00:01:13,898
With an adult: press a shell or a toy into modelling clay,

28
00:01:13,948 --> 00:01:15,043
then lift it off…

29
00:01:15,093 --> 00:01:17,316
your print is a miniature fossil!

30
00:01:18,112 --> 00:01:19,611
And where does the wind come from?

31
00:01:19,661 --> 00:01:20,572
The answer tomorrow.
